{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1744780,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":null,"paid":0,"title":"The Big Bull","festival_id":504454,"organization_id":675999,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-09-03T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-16T12:30:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/the-big-bull-techfest26-annual-technical-festival-of-sliet-sant-longowal-institute-of-engineering-and-techn-1744780","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>Select Your Registration Package<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Registration for the techFEST&rsquo;26 package is compulsory for accommodation and other perks, while participation in individual events is free*.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Note:<\/strong> Registration is mandatory for participation. Fee once paid is non-refundable.<\/p>\n<p><strong>About the Event:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>THE BIG BULL is an exciting team-based quiz challenge that combines knowledge, strategy, and decision-making. Participants compete in teams while answering questions from General Knowledge, Space, Basic Technical Concepts, Science and Technology, and Logical Thinking.<\/p>\n<p>Each team starts with a balance of <strong>5000 coins<\/strong>, which can be strategically used to purchase different lifelines during the game. Teams must carefully decide when to use their coins while maintaining their remaining balance throughout the event.<\/p>\n<p>The event tests participants' knowledge, logical thinking, teamwork, strategic decision-making, and ability to perform under time constraints.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Lifelines:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Teams can purchase the following lifelines using their coins:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>BULL'S HINT &ndash; 500 Coins:<\/strong> A useful hint related to the question will be provided to the team.<\/li>\n<li><strong>VISION BOOST &ndash; 1500 Coins:<\/strong> An image or visual clue related to the question will be displayed to help the team.<\/li>\n<li><strong>50-50 BLAST &ndash; 2000 Coins:<\/strong> Two incorrect options will be eliminated, leaving only two options to choose from.<\/li>\n<li><strong>BULL'S PASS &ndash; 2500 Coins:<\/strong> The team can skip the current question and move on to the next question.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Regulations:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Team Size:<\/strong> Each team will consist of 2&ndash;3 members.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Starting Balance:<\/strong> Every team will receive <strong>5000 coins<\/strong> at the beginning of the event.<\/li>\n<li>All teams will be seated separately.<\/li>\n<li>Every question will be displayed simultaneously on the main screen for all teams.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must discuss and submit their answer within the <strong>given time limit<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Lifelines can be purchased only using the team's available coins.<\/li>\n<li>A team cannot use a lifeline if it does not have sufficient coins.<\/li>\n<li>Each lifeline can be used according to the rules specified by the organizers.<\/li>\n<li>Questions will primarily cover General Knowledge, Space, Basic Technical Concepts, Science and Technology, and Logical Thinking.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must maintain their remaining coin balance throughout the game.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The event is open to <strong>only Diploma students (all years)<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>All participants must carry a <strong>valid college ID card<\/strong> during the event for verification purposes.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rewards &amp; Recognition:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Exciting prizes for the <strong>Top 3 Winners<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Certificates for all participants.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Certification Policy:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All participants will receive certificates.<\/li>\n<li>Winners will be awarded certificates and prizes based on the final results declared by the judges.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Important Note:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Judges' decisions will be final and binding.<\/li>\n<li>Bring your valid student ID and confirmation receipt.<\/li>\n<li>Report <strong>15 minutes before<\/strong> the event starts.<\/li>\n<li>Any unfair means, cheating, or inappropriate behavior may lead to disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>The organizers reserve the right to modify the rules, schedule, or any aspect of the event, with prior notice, in the best interest of the competition.<\/li>\n<li>All participants must follow the instructions given by the event coordinators.<\/li>\n<li>All participants must stay updated through official notices on the <strong>SLIET techFEST 2026 website<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Further modifications to the problem statement may be made based on subsequent analysis and requirements.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Registration Dates:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Registration Start:<\/strong> 3 September 2026<\/li>\n<li><strong>Registration End:<\/strong> 25 September 2026<\/li>\n<li><strong>For Further Query:<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Domain Advisor:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Raju Kumar<\/li>\n<li>2341023\/GCS<\/li>\n<li>6209681064<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Domain Coordinator:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Aisha Kumari<\/li>\n<li>2442003\/GCT<\/li>\n<li>6209681064<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Event Coordinator:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Swati Kumari<\/li>\n<li>2633017\/GEC<\/li>\n<li>6209681064<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Accommodation and Meals:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Registration for the techFEST&rsquo;26 package is compulsory for accommodation and other perks, while participation in individual events is free*.<\/strong><\/p>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":null,"registration_clicks":0,"user_id":27463276,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-08-26T23:12:07+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-04T16:36:43+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"c